A||||2||burdell1||Fusible Links
Z||000000||burdell1||06-17-99||01:47 PM||||Does anybody out there know how to repair fusible links? I was trying to fix my headlights so they go up and down and I ended up tearing apart one of them.
Z||000001||theogre||06-17-99||05:53 PM||||you don't repair them. they get cut out and a new one splicded with a crimp type connector.
Z||000002||Cooter||06-19-99||09:11 PM||||Another option to the fusible link wire is to just splice in an "inline fuse holder" that uses the blade fuses. I believe a 15 amp fuse for the headlight motors should be about right. Then if you toast one, just pop in a new fuse instead of cutting and splicing in more link wire.
